    "manifest_definition": "SHA-256 of the `shasum -a 256` manifest over exactly the source_files paths below, in the listed LC_ALL=C order, using repository-relative POSIX paths.",
    "manifest_scope": "Exactly the producer modules cellucid.prepare() executes: the cellucid entries sys.modules holds once cellucid.prepare is imported. Modules outside that set - the Jupyter viewer, the HTTP server, session bundles, the web cache, the command line - cannot reach the bytes prepare() writes, so pinning them reports a difference where the store has none. The builder recomputes the executed set on every run and refuses to build when prepare() reaches a module this list omits, so the list cannot silently stop covering the producer. Every path is named rather than matched by a directory pattern, so a producer file that is renamed or removed fails by name. The interpreter, the exact installed distribution set and the producer release are pinned separately by python_version, requirements_lock_sha256 and version.",
